  <section|Mathematical details and scope><label|mathematical-details-and-scope>

  The manuscript keeps the three terms separate. The witness term costs
  <verbatim|Tau(-1200000+150000)=Tau(-1050000)>. For the correction, the
  global product cap is <verbatim|Tau(650000)>, the healthy-set cap is
  <verbatim|Tau(-350000)>, and support size is at most <verbatim|Tau(1000)>.
  The exceptional-set tail contributes <verbatim|Tau(650000+1000-1200000)=Tau(-549000)>.
  Together with the witness term, each of the three summands is at most
  <verbatim|Tau(-31000)>; <verbatim|3\<leq\>Tau(1)> yields
  <verbatim|Tau(-30000)>.

  The source <verbatim|Mortal.funeral> proof uses the threshold-to-prism
  inequality, the treasury bound, and the plaquette/clip lower bound. The
  manuscript spells out the scalar scale comparison and applies it to the
  support union bound. The one-site action receipt and normalized transfer
  identity are displayed as explicit incoming hypotheses, not claimed as
  proved in this unit. The Crown witness-production route also remains
  upstream.

  <section|Audit><label|audit>

  Read-only source inspection used <verbatim|rg -n> and <verbatim|sed -n> on
  the paths in the crosswalk. No Lean source was edited. No Lean, TeX, or
  blueprint check was run.

